# Revisions to skip in `git blame` -- bulk, content-neutral rewrites only.
#
# Use with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# (GitHub honors this file automatically.)
#
# Sprint 61 Task 0 (line-ending normalization, 2026-08-17): `.gitattributes`
# was added to normalize line endings to LF. The follow-up
# `git add --renormalize .` produced ZERO changed files -- the repository was
# already LF-consistent in storage, and the constant "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warnings came from checkout-time conversion, not from mixed content.
# There is therefore NO renormalization commit to list here, and blame history
# is entirely unaffected. This file is kept in place so the next bulk
# formatting change (a repo-wide formatter run, a mass rename) has an obvious
# home rather than being added under time pressure.
#
# Format: one full 40-character SHA per line, with a comment saying what it was.
